                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6eed1c13-f504-4cb2-b2fe-7b910ae2e5c5",
                                "sense_id": "ccdc280f-bf01-3a74-a920-f34dd31ed974",
                                "text": "[…] when the seed surrenders, it becomes a tree. Seeds that don’t surrender their “seedness” only wither up and blow away."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "327e6d4f-89ba-3598-83a7-e5937211b712",
                        "entry_id": "01f4bcb8-2331-33bc-936d-9e5474bbdca8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Seedtime."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fc2f0cf5-53cd-4717-a093-4a6edc426a42",
                                "sense_id": "327e6d4f-89ba-3598-83a7-e5937211b712",
                                "text": "As those that feed grow full, as blossoming time\nThat from the seedness the bare fallow brings\nTo teeming foison, even so her plenteous womb\nExpresseth his full tilth and husbandry."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0ba301b2-b753-419a-b3bb-d48274a3d3e7",
                                "sense_id": "327e6d4f-89ba-3598-83a7-e5937211b712",
                                "text": "[…] there be certaine little wormes breeding in the root, that do eat it: which happeneth by occasion of much raine falling immediatly after the seednesse, especially, when some sudden heat and drowth ensueth therupon […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cd2b158a-48b2-4366-969b-e032aaf515b2",
                                "sense_id": "327e6d4f-89ba-3598-83a7-e5937211b712",
                                "text": "[…] how does God admonish us of the value of time, by so constructing things, as that opportunities once let slip, i.e. time wasted, are never to be redeemed, do what we will to repair our folly! A seedness suffered to escape, and the harvest for the year irrecoverable […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
